<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75780" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδετέρ-ωσε</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to neither of two sides,
				neither way</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδ᾽ ἄρα τε
				προκυλίνδεται οὐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				14.18
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ. κλινόμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					945
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ. ῥέπει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					2.1.11
				</span></i>
			. (Perh. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδ᾽ ἑτέρωσε</span> shd.
			be written everywhere.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
